  <h1>The Collaborative Advocate Foundation</h1>
  <p class="header-info">501(c)(3) Nonprofit Organization | EIN: 41-3618503</p>
  <p class="header-info">17912 Stefano Drive, Pflugerville, TX 78660</p>
  <p class="period">Leadership &amp; Key Staff Overview</p>
  <p class="header-info">Prepared for: Rare Impact Fund &mdash; Strengthening the Nonclinical Youth Mental Health Workforce</p>

  <h2>Executive Leadership</h2>

  <div class="person">
  <p class="person-name">Dr. Terry Flood, DHA</p>
  <p class="person-title">Founder &amp; Chief Executive Officer</p>
  <p class="person-org">The Collaborative Advocate Foundation (TCAF)</p>
  <ul>
  <li>Doctor of Healthcare Administration with expertise in implementation science, community health systems, and workforce development</li>
  <li>U.S. Army veteran &mdash; Bronze Star recipient (x2) with extensive leadership experience in high-stakes operational environments</li>
  <li>Architect of RPLICE (Reach, Program, Legitimacy, Implementation, Community, Evaluation) &mdash; a proprietary implementation science engine operationalizing CFIR 2.0 and RE-AIM frameworks for program fidelity and continuous improvement</li>
  <li>Serves on the Pflugerville ISD School Health Advisory Council (SHAC), providing direct connection to youth-serving systems in Central Texas</li>
  <li>Designed TCAF's 24-platform technology ecosystem spanning workforce development, health equity, benefits navigation, and community data intelligence</li>
  <li>Developer of the culturally responsive workforce readiness curriculum currently serving youth through PfISD partnership (20 lessons, 5 modules)</li>
  <li>Expertise in social determinants of health, GIS-based community analysis, and data-driven program design using 8 federal data sources (CDC PLACES, SVI, Census ACS, USDA, BLS, SAMHSA, HUD, FBI UCR)</li>
  </ul>
  </div>

  <hr>

  <div class="person">
  <p class="person-name">Meredith Sisnett</p>
  <p class="person-title">Community Coordinator</p>
  <p class="person-org">The Collaborative Advocate Foundation (TCAF)</p>
  <ul>
  <li>Contract Management Specialist III at the City of Austin Housing Department &mdash; Displacement Prevention division, with expertise in contract oversight, compliance monitoring, and coordination with housing service providers</li>
  <li>Former Organizational Development &amp; Training Specialist at the City of Austin, facilitating New Hire Orientation and Management Training programs</li>
  <li>Recognized by NAACP President Nelson Linder for community service and dedication to helping others</li>
  <li>Recognized by MEASURE President Meme Styles for Community Engagement and Philanthropic efforts</li>
  <li>Experience in community engagement, program coordination, and partnership development across Austin's nonprofit and civic sectors</li>
  <li>Brings deep understanding of housing stability, displacement prevention, and social services navigation &mdash; critical context for supporting youth and families facing mental health challenges rooted in housing insecurity and economic instability</li>
  <li>Coordinates TCAF's community outreach, participant recruitment, and integration of community voice into program design</li>
  </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Strategic Partners &mdash; Key Staff Involved in This Project</h2>

  <div class="person">
  <p class="person-name">Eric Hargrave</p>
  <p class="person-title">Chief Executive Officer</p>
  <p class="person-org">Hargrave Innovative Solutions (HIS)</p>
  <ul>
  <li>21-year U.S. Marine Corps veteran with expertise in government contracting, acquisitions, compliance, and program management</li>
  <li>Lead consultant and business developer for nonprofits including Fountain of Life Ministries &mdash; spearheaded funding strategies, grant development, and community programming</li>
  <li>Extensive experience in strategic planning, risk management, federal procurement, and contract oversight</li>
  <li>Provides TCAF with grant administration, compliance support, and workforce development program infrastructure</li>
  </ul>
  </div>

  <hr>

  <div class="person">
  <p class="person-name">Dr. Regina Whitelow</p>
  <p class="person-title">Chief Executive Officer</p>
  <p class="person-org">Universal Spectrum</p>
  <ul>
  <li>Award-winning grant writer and business strategist with a track record of securing millions in funding for nonprofit organizations</li>
  <li>Specialist in financial sustainability, strategic planning, and program development</li>
  <li>Successfully secured funding for Rockford Black Chamber of Commerce, Philadelphia Missionary Baptist Church youth programs, and multiple nonprofit and small business clients</li>
  <li>Expertise in bid preparation, compliance reporting, grant administration, and funding acquisition</li>
  </ul>
  </div>

  <hr>

  <div class="person">
  <p class="person-name">Jamaika McAdams</p>
  <p class="person-title">Chief Administrative Officer</p>
  <p class="person-org">Hargrave Innovative Solutions (HIS)</p>
  <ul>
  <li>Retired U.S. Army Administrator and HR Specialist with expertise in business operations, personnel management, and contract compliance</li>
  <li>Skilled in policy development, grant administration, and financial tracking</li>
  <li>Experience coordinating multi-agency partnerships and workforce development initiatives</li>
  <li>Provides operational and administrative support for TCAF's program delivery and grant compliance</li>
  </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Combined Team Qualifications</h2>

  <ul>
  <li><strong>50+ years combined experience</strong> across healthcare administration, military service, grant writing, program management, government contracting, and community development</li>
  <li><strong>Three military veterans</strong> (U.S. Army, U.S. Marine Corps) &mdash; authentic connection to veteran communities and disciplined operational approach</li>
  <li><strong>Black-led organization</strong> &mdash; leadership reflects the historically marginalized communities TCAF serves</li>
  <li><strong>City of Austin government experience</strong> &mdash; direct knowledge of municipal housing, displacement prevention, and community services systems</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation science expertise</strong> &mdash; Dr. Flood's RPLICE engine provides the evidence-based evaluation framework that ensures program fidelity and measurable outcomes</li>
  <li><strong>Grant management capacity</strong> &mdash; HIS and Universal Spectrum bring proven grant writing, compliance, and financial management infrastructure</li>
  <li><strong>Community rootedness</strong> &mdash; Pflugerville headquarters, PfISD SHAC membership, NAACP recognition, and established relationships across Central Texas nonprofit, education, and civic sectors</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="section-note">This leadership overview is provided as part of TCAF's Letter of Intent submission to the Rare Impact Fund's "Strengthening the Nonclinical Youth Mental Health Workforce" program (April 2026).</p>

